  "body": "Charles Nelson currently waits away from the Glessner-front Brougham. This brings the existing coachman beside its waiting team on the Prairie Avenue parkway, between the trees and clear of the principal walking strip. His identity, all four seasonal routines, original short-break location and stable-door tour mark are retained. The other seven household records remain byte exact.\n\nVisible tour hosts use real approach and return routes. An unavailable route waits and retries; narration waits for the guide to arrive, with Next/End still available. Actual camera cuts may hand off a host before the first destination frame. Menu/Resume retains the host. Running household errands and tour guides keep ownership of their paths/callbacks: a tour waits for an errand, while Greet/Stroll/door actions refuse a held guide. End while waiting never takes the person later.\n\nValidation:\n- Current head `11d4bb29bb4cf14bf20e2796da4b4b99c1273a4c` normally merges latest DEV `b4eb1cbf0fa557ba98059846c60bf46978a6b92c`, preserving the newly merged picture-review work. Its two derived conflicts were regenerated by the canonical owners. All 1,088 existing DEV Liberty rows are exact; only the coachman entry is added. Canonical owner/self-tests passed in 82.27 s; source-use/manifest and all six focused day/round/household/jaunt suites passed in 21.25 s under unchanged SUP120/floors with complete cleanup.\n- Both pre-fix errand/guide ownership counterexamples reproduced their expected failures. The fixed source passes, including busy\u2192free handoff and End while busy.\n- Earlier head `2c9df872` passed all eight gate partitions, aggregate gate, humans, moving frames and phone upload release. Those are results for that head. Complete hosted checks are running again on current `11d4`; they remain mandatory before merge. Complete local preflight was not passed in this sparse asset checkout. The full local conflict resolver would first publish the entire missing asset mirror, exceeding the retained 512 MiB disk floor, so only the two canonical owners were run locally; no full derived-tail pass is claimed.\n- [Original image and complete bounded physical evidence](https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago-evidence/tree/50d4bcf5f96c648aa70f18041df2c9c4493ddcc1/evidence/transport/coachman-placement-2026-11-10/pr1917-2c9df8-bounded-post) are explicitly bound to the local `2c9` overlay fixture, whose saved banner says `9d`. Local visual review found the coachman, horses and walking strip clearly visible. This is not a live deployed `11d4` image. The sampled Balanced reading passed the stricter earlier limits: 2,052,390/2,625,000 triangles and 3,311/7,800 draws.\n\nThe image retains the native engage-look prompt. The post-gesture screenshot timed out at its unchanged 90 s cap, so that strict observer remains NONPASS (482.77s, cleanup complete, zero owned children). Its 29 aborted native texture requests are retained; actual page/HTTP/server errors were zero. No clean post-gesture, full-world or photographic pass is claimed.\n\nThe finite physical probe measured all 1,466/1,476 actual LOD1 foot vertices and confirmed both terrain cut materials discard the raw field underneath. Soles remain about 27 mm above the drawn parkway; a separate ground-support correction is prepared, not hidden with a per-person offset. Original horse contact limits passed for that finite pose, and coachman/team bounds remain disjoint. This leaves broader grounding, continuous contact and photographic acceptance open.\n\nT-2795 remains open. Boarding, a coachman conversation offering a ride, reins and seated passengers remain on the existing transport tickets. This is DEV integration only; no production promotion or MAIN publisher change.\n\n![Source-bound coachman placement; local `2c9` fixture, native prompt retained](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kevinrhaas/chicago-evidence/50d4bcf5f96c648aa70f18041df2c9c4493ddcc1/evidence/transport/coachman-placement-2026-11-10/pr1917-2c9df8-bounded-post/image07/candidate-ensemble-before-ui.png)\n\n[Current integration and canonical-owner checkpoint](https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago-evidence/tree/dae9ad71e2d7893696ff4dfcbb3fe96de231f1cc/evidence/transport/coachman-placement-2026-11-10/pr1917-integration-11d4bb) keeps current-head pending checks separate from the completed earlier-head checks.\n",
